course: dictionary
lesson: 2255
title: One word, many meanings: crawl
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Crawl is a good example. A baby crawls on hands and knees, a worm crawls along the ground, and a swimmer does the front crawl. The context clues show you which meaning you need.
explain: «For example, a girl in Texas finds a marble on the rug where her baby brother crawls.» Babies do not usually walk yet, so crawls means moves on hands and knees here. Try the swap: "where her baby brother moves on hands and knees" still makes sense, so the meaning is right.
explain: Sometimes the situation gives the clue. In fire safety, you are told to get down low and crawl to the exit, because smoke rises and the cleaner air is near the floor. Here crawl means moving low and slowly, close to the ground. Ask yourself what the words around it are doing.
fact: Crawl can be a verb or a noun: you can crawl, or you can do a crawl in swimming.
fact: To crawl means to move on your hands and knees, as babies do.
fact: Insects, worms and snakes crawl along the ground, usually slowly.
fact: To crawl can also mean to go very slowly, like traffic in a jam.
fact: The front crawl is a fast swimming stroke with the arms going over the head one at a time.
exercise: «Traffic was at a crawl on the motorway all morning.» What does crawl mean here? | *To go very slowly, like traffic in a jam | To jump high over the road | To swim fast with the arms over the head | To move on hands and knees
exercise: «The room was crawling with ants after the picnic.» What does crawling with mean? | Very cold and wet | Empty and clean | *Full of crawling creatures | Covered in fresh paint
exercise: Ruby learns the front crawl at swimming lessons. What is the front crawl? | A way of climbing a tree | A slow walk along the sand | *A fast swimming stroke with the arms going over the head one at a time | A game played with a ball
test: «The Mole panics, runs blindly, falls over things, and at last crawls into the hollow of an old beech tree, trembling.» Which word could replace crawls without changing the meaning? | dances | shouts | *creeps | sleeps
test: «Time crawled by as we waited for the bus.» What does crawled mean here? | Swam fast in the sea | *Seemed to pass very slowly | Moved on hands and knees | Ran away quickly
exam: «A girl in Texas finds a marble on the rug where her baby brother crawls.» Which meaning of crawl fits best here? | To swim the front crawl | To go slowly, like traffic in a jam | *To move on hands and knees, as babies do | To be full of creatures
